Putting the pieces together: generate_filter_pattern starts from a near-gray random 200×200 image and applies 30 gradient-ascent steps of amplitude 10. deprocess_image then standardizes, rescales, clips, center-crops and casts the result into a displayable uint8 image. A filter visualization is the endpoint of a short optimization in pixel space. The raw result is an unbounded float tensor, so it must be mapped back to the [0, 255] range, with the unreliable border removed, before it can be shown. With the step function ready, **section 10.2.4** assembles the full procedure into a function that takes a filter index and returns the pattern that maximizes that filter's activation in the target layer (`block3_sepconv1`).

